# D26 axis: op=Shl · route=B (Result-capture) · NEG (rejected at check) · int64.
# The check-lane rejects shift-fallible at a `Result[T, ArithError]` capture
# destination with `E_ShiftFallibleRouteBNotYetImplemented`. Route A (throws-
# propagate via auto-infer) still works for shifts — see
# `c1_d26_shift_shl_ok.gg` / `c1_d26_shift_shr_ok.gg` — so the reject is
# scoped to Route B only. The follow-up in TODO.md (D26 shift-fallible Route
# B lowering gap) extends `FaultableBinOp` LIR + `lower_fallible_arith_binop`
# to accept Shl/Shr with a new FaultOp category, at which point this reject
# retires and the sibling `known_gaps/c1_d26_shift_capture_type_mismatch.gg`
# graduates to a positive fixture.
#
# RED-verify: BEFORE the check-lane reject landed, this fixture compiled +
# ran and SIGSEGV'd (exit 139) because the lowering emitted plain-int shift
# result stored into a `Result[int, ArithError]` slot; the caller's match
# read garbage bytes as the discriminant. Silent type-confusion miscompile,
# both backends. AFTER: check-lane refuses with the intended diagnostic;
# nothing lowers.
void main():
    int a = 4
    int b = 2
    Result[int, ArithError] r = a <<! b
    match r:
        case Ok(v): print(v)
        case Error(e): print(-1)
